 26 
will be limited across all resource types: 17.6 GW of gas in the queue was unlikely to be 
built and therefore counted only upgrades from old projects and projects already 
under construction; Renewables were estimated using a logistic regression model 
trained on historical queue data to predict the completion rate from queue entry to in-
service, which is relatively low. The individual capacity of renewables is adjusted 
downward because renewables cannot reliably supply load, and these capacity 
contribution values decrease further as more intermittent resources are integrated 
into the grid. On the demand side, the four R report in 2023 has yet to be updated with 
the following years’ load forecast. Since 2023, the load forecast has been increasing. 
PJM's 2023 forecast assumed a compounded annual growth rate of 0.4-0.8%.
