MISO defined "shovel-ready" through eligibility gates. ERAS required a commercial 
operation date no more than three years from submission, with a three-year grace 
period; location within a local resource zone with an identified need; 100% site control; 
and an executed off-take agreement, or a self-supply acknowledgment for utilities. 
The requested interconnection service cannot exceed 150% of the maximum capacity 
